matroskadec: option to read the Cues while opening and export them

A player that serves a Matroska file in pieces (subtitle cues fetched by
byte range, keyframes read on their own) needs the file's index with the
fields libavformat parses and then drops: CueRelativePosition, which says
where a block starts inside its cluster, and CueDuration. It also needs
each track's ContentEncoding to undo zlib or header stripping on a block it
reads itself. Without them it parses the Cues and Tracks a second time.

export_cues (off by default) reads the Cues while the file opens, through
the SeekHead as a seek would, instead of on the first seek, and exports
three read-only values on the demuxer's private context:

  cue_points       int64 array, five values per CueTrackPositions whose
                   track became a stream, in file order: stream index,
                   CueTime in segment ticks, cluster position from the
                   start of the file, CueRelativePosition and CueDuration
                   (-1 where absent). Empty unless the Cues parsed whole.
  track_coding     int64 array, per stream with a ContentEncodings element,
                   in stream order: stream index, number of ContentEncoding
                   elements, then the first one's ContentEncodingType,
                   ContentEncodingScope as coded, ContentCompAlgo, the size
                   of ContentCompSettings and its bytes, one value each.
  timestamp_scale  uint64, nanoseconds per segment tick.

They are read with av_opt_get_array() and av_opt_get_int() on
AVFormatContext.priv_data and freed with the context. The index the
demuxer builds for seeking is unchanged; without the option nothing is
exported and the Cues are still read on the first seek.

